    "note": "Duration is 300 s under Amendment A1 (see amendment). The approved draft said 180 s; verified trial counts from the downloaded events.tsv files showed 180 s cannot meet the trial floors (5 of 20 subjects below 15 valid targets), so the excerpt was lengthened to 300 s with floors unchanged. Still a short excerpt of a ~8-10 min task."
  },
  "amendment": {
    "id": "A1",
    "status": "PENDING USER APPROVAL - run must not launch before approval",
    "change": "Excerpt duration 180 s -> 300 s. All other frozen decisions unchanged.",
    "evidence": "Valid target/standard counts (correct trials, RT 200-1000 ms) computed from each subject's downloaded events.tsv with the frozen trial rules. At 180 s, 5 subjects fail the >=15 valid-target floor: sub-004 (11 targets, 56 standards), sub-008 (14), sub-013 (14), sub-014 (13), sub-022 (13). At 240 s sub-004 still fails (13). At 300 s all 20 pass: 18-32 valid targets, 95-138 valid standards. Per-subject counts are pinned in source.files (valid_targets_180s/300s, valid_standards_180s/300s)."
  },
  "trial_rules": {
    "rt_min_seconds": 0.2,
    "rt_max_seconds": 1.0,
    "correct_only": true,
    "min_valid_targets": 15,
    "min_valid_standards": 60,
    "event_codes": "Two-digit stimulus codes; tens digit = block target letter (1=A..5=E), ones digit = shown letter. Target when tens == ones (11, 22, 33, 44, 55); otherwise standard. Responses: 201 = correct, 202 = error.",
    "relabeling": "Target codes -> '11', standard codes -> '31', response events dropped after correctness/RT filtering. Required because pop_pipecompare 'events' accepts one condition per event type and cannot express target = 5 codes / standard = 20 codes. Original codes, correctness and RTs are preserved in input.mat trials.* and source.json, so the relabeling is fully auditable.",
    "epoch_fit_rule": "Stimuli with onset < 0.2 s or > duration - 0.8 s are excluded so the full -200..800 ms epoch fits inside the excerpt.",
    "fdt_parsing": "EEGLAB .fdt is little-endian float32 written column-major (time-major on disk); reshape Fortran-order (nbchan x pnts, order='F'). A C-order reshape scrambles channels into white noise (verified on sub-001: flat spectrum above 30 Hz, no power below; Fortran order restores 1/f spectrum and neighbour correlation ~0.98).",
    "dc_offsets": "Recordings carry large DC offsets and slow drift (sub-001 Pz std ~86-108 uV raw, ~9 uV after the paper's 0.1 Hz high-pass). Fetch subtracts the per-channel mean over the excerpt only; high-pass filtering is left to the pipelines under test (the Standard search and both fixed arms include a 0.1 Hz high-pass). The tool's blink reference is drift-immune by design (baseline-subtracted window means with robust z-scores; sampleHits subtracts a 1 s moving median)."
  },
